-- title:
--   Points reading a non-node place have non-supersingular j
-- statement:
--   The statement is set in the following arithmetic frame. Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$. Let $k(A)$ denote the residue field of $A$, and write $\mathcal M_{M'}=$ `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` for the subfield of $k(A)$-Laurent series generated by the reductions of the $q$-expansions of $j$ and $j(M'z)$, and $\bar F_{M'}=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` for the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field inside $\mathbb Q$-Laurent series. A finset $W$ of places of $\mathcal M_{M'}$ over $k(A)$ is given together with `hW`, which says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places, i.e. those places $w$ that are rational, affine geometric, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(j^{\mathrm{geom}})\in$ `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)` (the set of $j$-values such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve with that invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion affine point). The inclusion `hle` asserts $\bar F_{M'}\le \bar F:=$ `fieldBar q M'`, the latter being the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the $\Gamma_H$-modular function field of level $q^2M'$ with $H=$ `levelH q M'` the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$.
--
--   Next, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\bar F_{M'}$ to $\mathcal M_{M'}$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\bar F_{M'}$ contracting to $A$ on $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, with a surjective residue homomorphism onto $\mathcal M_{M'}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$, such that every nonzero element becomes integral with nonzero residue after scaling by a constant, and a place map preserving degrees and compatible with divisors of functions. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that a Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series lies in $\bar F_{M'}$ is $R_0$-integral, with $R_0$-residue the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. An element $\zeta$ of `Idx q` (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) is fixed, and two families of valuation subrings of $\bar F$ are given: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ indexed by the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$, and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$.
--
--   The Igusa group of hypotheses: `hIg_inf` describes $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, $\infty=$ `lineInfty q` being the class of $(1,0)$, as the Gauss-type ring of those $f$ for which there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f\cdot y=x$ coefficientwise over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; `hIg` gives, for each line $\ell$, some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $\mathrm{redQ}\,\gamma\cdot\infty=\ell$ and $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj` asserts injectivity of $\ell\mapsto O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$; `hIg_perm` asserts that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family. The supersingular group: `hSS_A` says that for each $s$ an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ has its image in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ precisely when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over` says that if $f$ is $R_0$-integral and has non-negative order at every place of $\bar F_{M'}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the $j$-element (the image of the $q$-expansion `jq` under the coefficient embedding) has non-negative order, and if the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals the value at $s$ of that $R_0$-residue the difference between the image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix` says each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along all `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; `hSS_tr` provides for each $s$ an element $t\in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that $t-a$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a\in A$.
--
--   Further, $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from $\bar F$ to the $\Gamma_H$-function field `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` over $k(A)$ (same data as above without the place map), with `hR` identifying $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, and `hR₀O` saying that $R_0$-integrality of $f\in\bar F_{M'}$ is equivalent to its image lying in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$. A local datum is given: $\pi\in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$. A small-constants datum is given: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that the contraction $A\cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hdvr`, `hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`), has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hκ`). An auxiliary prime datum is given: a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally a finite layer is given: a finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ cut out by $A$ (`hA₁`), which is a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for `fieldBar q M'` regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}\to\bar F$, and quantifies over every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0\subseteq\bar F$ subject to four conditions: the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $\bar F$; $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; a linear disjointness condition, namely that for every finite extension $K'/k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$, and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\bar F$ with all $a_i$ in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the vanishing of $\sum_i c_i a_i$ forces all $a_i=0$; and that every element of $\bar F$ whose underlying Laurent series has rational coefficients, i.e. lies in the range of `coeffEmb`, belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   Write $T_1$ for the join, inside $\bar F$, of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_1$. The statement quantifies further over an $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map is compatible with $A_1\subseteq K_1\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}\to\bar F$, over an element $j_1\in T_1$ whose image in $\bar F$ is the $j$-element of $\bar F_{M'}$ described above, with $j_1\ne 0$, and over a finset $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of places of the $\Gamma_H$-function field over $k(A)$ for which there exists a ring homomorphism $j:\mathcal M_{M'}\to$ `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` such that, first, every $R_0$-integral $f$ has its image in $\bar F$ lying in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $R$-residue equal to $j$ applied to the $R_0$-residue of $f$, and second, $Q\in N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ holds precisely when there is $s\in W$ with $g$ in the valuation subring of $s$ if and only if $j(g)$ is in the valuation subring of $Q$, for all $g\in\mathcal M_{M'}$.
--
--   On the scheme $\mathfrak X_1=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two affine charts $X_{\mathrm{fin}}=\mathrm{Spec}\,B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $X_\infty=\mathrm{Spec}\,B_\infty$, where $B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ (resp. $B_\infty$) is the subalgebra of elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$ (resp. over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$), six local abbreviations are introduced: `InStalk x f` (for every $y$ in either chart mapping to $x$ there are $g,h$ in the corresponding chart algebra with $h\notin\mathfrak p_y$ and $fh=g$, i.e. $f$ lies in the local ring at $y$); `InMax x f` (the same with in addition $g\in\mathfrak p_y$); `Centred P x` for a place $P$ of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ ($P$ is rational and every $f$ with `InStalk x f` is $P$-integral with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$, this value lying in the maximal ideal of $A$ exactly when `InMax x f` holds); `GoodPt x` (five clauses: $x$ lies over the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$; $x$ is closed, every $y$ with $x\rightsquigarrow y$ being equal to $x$; on each of the two charts, every chart element whose image in $\bar F$ is a nonunit of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in $\mathfrak p_y$ for every $y$ over $x$; and for every $y$ in the finite chart over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:B_{\mathrm{fin}}\to\Omega$ with kernel $\mathfrak p_y$, the value $\varphi(\,$`jChartFin`$\,)$ is not in `ssJSet q Ω`); `Reads x Q` (every $f$ with `InStalk x f` has its image in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, with $R$-residue in the valuation subring of $Q$, and that residue is a nonunit there exactly when `InMax x f`); and `OffBranch x` (for every line $\ell\ne\infty$ and every $y$ over $x$ in either chart there is a chart element outside $\mathfrak p_y$ whose image is a nonunit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$). Of these, only `InStalk`, `InMax` and `Reads` enter the assertion.
--
--   The assertion itself: for every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ which lies over the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$, is closed in the sense that $x\rightsquigarrow y$ implies $y=x$, and satisfies on both charts the condition that every chart element whose image in $\bar F$ is a nonunit of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ belongs to $\mathfrak p_y$ for all $y$ over $x$, and for every place $Q$ of the $\Gamma_H$-function field over $k(A)$ with $Q\notin N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ and `Reads x Q`: for every $y$ in the finite chart with $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}(y)=x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:B_{\mathrm{fin}}\to\Omega$ with $\ker\varphi=\mathfrak p_y$, the element $\varphi(\,$`jChartFin`$\,)$ does not lie in `ssJSet q Ω`; equivalently, some elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has a nonzero $q$-torsion point. Thus the four conditions imposed on $x$ are the first four clauses of `GoodPt`, and the conclusion is its fifth clause; only the finite chart occurs in the conclusion.
--
--   This is the contrapositive of the characterisation of the Igusa nodes $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$: a closed point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model lying on the $\infty$-Igusa branch and reading a place outside $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ cannot lie above a supersingular $j$-invariant, since over a supersingular value the read place would correspond to a supersingular place $s\in W$ and hence be a node. It supplies the supersingularity-avoidance clause of `GoodPt` and is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_goodPt_and_offBranch_and_reads_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_goodPt_and_offBranch_and_reads_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel) in the construction of the semistable integral model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ over $A$.
